            <ArticleTitle>Diagnosis of obstructive coronary artery disease by cardiogoniometry: a field test in a real-life setting.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>420-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.jelectrocard.2015.01.012</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0022-0736(15)00045-X</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Cardiogoniometry is an electrocardiographic and vectorcardiographic method utilizing computer-assisted analysis of cardiac potentials focusing on T-wave abnormalities resulting from myocardial malperfusion. We describe a case of diagnosis of obstructive coronary artery disease with this method and discuss the possible implications for the clinical setting.</AbstractText>
